{{DISPLAYTITLE:Golden Knight (Merge Tactics)}}{{Protection}}{{MagicWords}}{{Merge Tactics Infobox|Cost=5|Trait1=Noble|Trait2=Assassin|Type=Troop|ReleaseDate=30 June 2025}}{{Quote|Dashes to the lowest HP enemy after defeating an enemy and deals bonus Damage}}

The Golden Knight is a [[Cards|card]] that belongs in the {{Trait|Noble}} and {{Trait|Assassin}} [[:Category:Cards by Trait|traits]]. It spawns a single-target melee [[:Category:Merge Tactics Troop Cards|troop]] with high hitpoints, damage, and attack speed. Upon defeating an enemy troop, he dashes to the troop with the lowest hitpoints, dealing bonus damage. The Golden Knight takes the appearance of a man who has blue eyes, golden hair and eyebrows, is outfitted in gilded breastplate, gauntlets, chainmail and a brown belt, and wields a large sword. A Golden Knight card costs 5 {{Icon|I=Golden Elixir}} to deploy.

==Strategy==
*Golden Knight is a very deadly [[:Category:Merge Tactics Troop Cards|troop]], as his dashes can easily shred a player's defenses due to it targeting the weakest troops first. At higher merge levels, his dash bonus damage scales exponentially, dealing extremely high damage at 3 or 4 stars. A chain dash attack occurs when the Golden Knight repeatedly defeats enemies with his dash.
**One way to counter the Golden Knight is to have him locked onto a tank, such as the [[Skeleton King/Merge Tactics|Skeleton King]], and defeat him quickly, mitigating his dash. Stun effects are also a good way of preventing him initiate his dash or stop his chain dash attack.
**Because of this, great ways to increase Golden Knight's performance include troops with stun attacks, {{Trait|Noble}}'s damage increase (the player must play him in the backline), and {{Trait|Undead}}'s enemy hitpoint reduction. The former also allows the player to access other [[:Category:Cards by Trait|traits]] that can benefit the player's team in another way.
*His {{Trait|Noble}} trait allows him to take less damage when placed in the frontline, increasing his survivability, or deal more damage when placed in the backline, increasing his chances of activating his dash, defeating an unit with his dash, and causing chain attacks with his dash.
*His {{Trait|Assassin}} trait allows him to target backline troops, which are usually frailer units, allowing him to use his dash effectively. The critical chance and critical damage increases also aid him in dashing more times, as well as defeating enemies with the dash to cause chain attacks. Due to this, he and other {{Trait|Assassin}} troops are great counters to set-ups who rely on backline troops as their main source of damage, as well as [[Elixir Collector/Merge Tactics|Elixir Collector]] and [[X-Bow/Merge Tactics|X-Bow]].
**When both of those traits are active, the player can play Golden Knight in the backline to significantly increase his damage. However, he can also be played in the frontline to increase his survivability, as he'll take less damage.

