==Trivia==
*The word "''Knight''" comes from the German "''Knecht''", meaning servant or vassal. Originally, knights were associated with mounted warriors, later being considered a class of lower nobility, until eventually, knighthood had become associated with the ideals of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chivalry chivalry], a code of conduct for the perfect courtly Christian warrior. Often, a knight was a vassal who served as an elite fighter or a bodyguard for a lord, with payment in the form of land holdings.
**In the Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Golden Knight's name translates to "Golden Armored Knight".
**The Golden Knight is 1 of 10 [[Merge Tactics]] [[:Category:Merge Tactics Troop Cards|troops]] associated with nobility, with the others being [[Knight/Merge Tactics|Knight]], [[Musketeer/Merge Tactics|Musketeer]], [[Royal Giant/Merge Tactics|Royal Giant]], [[Prince/Merge Tactics|Prince]], [[Mega Knight/Merge Tactics|Mega Knight]], [[Princess/Merge Tactics|Princess]], [[Royal Ghost/Merge Tactics|Royal Ghost]],  [[Skeleton King/Merge Tactics|Skeleton King]], and the [[Archer Queen/Merge Tactics|Archer Queen]].
*The Golden Knight is tied with [[Mini P.E.K.K.A./Merge Tactics|Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Goblins/Merge Tactics|Goblin]], [[Barbarians/Merge Tactics|Barbarian]], [[Valkyrie/Merge Tactics|Valkyrie]], [[P.E.K.K.A./Merge Tactics|P.E.K.K.A.]], Prince, [[Electro Giant/Merge Tactics|Electro Giant]], Mega Knight, Royal Ghost, [[Bandit/Merge Tactics|Bandit]], [[Goblin Machine/Merge Tactics|Goblin Machine]], Skeleton King, [[Monk/Merge Tactics|Monk]], and the [[Skeletons/Merge Tactics|Skeleton]] for the shortest range out of all Merge Tactics troops, with a range of 1 hex.

